    "fileId": 14437,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Subtyping of resected morphologically undifferentiated non-small cell carcinoma (formerly large cell carcinoma)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Giulio Rossi",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.85pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Tumour type</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 354.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"473\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Immunohistochemistry findings</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Adenocarcinoma, solid&nbsp;subtype<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 354.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"473\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive TTF1 and/or napsin&nbsp;A and/or mucin</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative (or focal staining in scattered tumour cells) p40, p63<sup>b</sup>, CK5/6</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Non-keratinizing squamous&nbsp;cell carcinoma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 354.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"473\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative TTF1, napsin&nbsp;A, mucin</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffusely positive p40, p63<sup>b</sup>, CK5/6</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Adenosquamous carcinoma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 354.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"473\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive adenosquamous and squamous markers in geographically distinct cell populations, each representing &ge;&nbsp;10% of tumour cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Large cell carcinoma (null&nbsp;immunophenotype)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 354.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"473\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive cytokeratins</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative lineage-specific markers</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 148.85pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"198\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Large cell carcinoma (unclear&nbsp;immunophenotype)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 354.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"473\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive cytokeratins</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unusual immunoprofiles</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>In cases where there is morphological evidence of either squamous cell carcinoma or adenocarcinoma, immunohistochemistry is not needed to assess undifferentiated areas.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>b</sup>p63 (4A4) can rarely be diffusely positive in some TTF1-positive tumours&nbsp;&ndash; these should be classified as adenocarcinomas.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
